# /etc/conf/modreg.d/gayle -- the gayle module package's defaults
# (amix-dlm C3-5 sec 1): one `param <name>=<value>` per default other than
# the module's own, `disable` to ship it off.  None: the package ships the
# module's own defaults, so interrupts are on (intr=1: interrupt I/O after a
# self-test at boot, polled I/O if the test fails) on both lines.  The
# switch back to polled I/O is the line
#   param intr=0
# in /etc/conf/modreg.local.d/gayle, which no package owns (local settings
# belong there), then kbootset build and commit.
